=== Course Overview
This course delves into the critical mathematical foundations essential for developing advanced artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It covers advanced mathematics topics that are crucial for modern AI, such as linear algebra (e.g., matrix operations and singular value decomposition), probability theory (e.g., Markov chains), optimization theory (e.g., gradient descent and second-order methods), and information theory (e.g., entropy and KL divergence). This course is designed for students who already have a basic understanding of mathematics and want to enhance their skills for AI-driven applications.

/This course is one of two sessions of AIE6001. The course materials are based on those developed by [https://walterbabyrudin.github.io/course.html Prof. Jie Wang]./

==== Prerequisites
Students should be comfortable with introductory calculus, linear algebra, and probability. Prior exposure to machine learning is helpful but not required. Mathematical maturity and a willingness to work through derivations are expected.


